0..70 Comment "// The manifold that deploys the migration model across two processes."
71..73 Comment "//"
74..151 Comment "// A manifold binds a program\'s worlds onto sites, so one program runs as two"
152..201 Comment "// processes without naming either in its source."
202..204 Comment "//"
205..278 Comment "// This one deploys the migration model beside it and places `far` at the"
279..354 Comment "// site it imports, whose model holds its key and socket. `near`, where the"
355..431 Comment "// entry runs, is placed nowhere: it is the process that runs `main`. `gandr"
432..502 Comment "// run --manifold` and `gandr host --manifold` read it as the `--world"
503..581 Comment "// far=<key>@<ip:port>` it desugars to, and `gandr check` of it resolves `far`"
582..614 Comment "// against the program\'s worlds."
615..617 Comment "//"
618..681 Comment "// - see: `two-processes.site.gandr` — the site `far` runs at"
682..740 Comment "// - see: `two-processes.gandr` — the program it deploys"
741..809 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-driver/tests/net.rs` — the two processes"
811..871 Comment "// The deployment theories, from `std.manifold` by its path."
